id: pm-rl-taj8
title: "pm rl compare: a metric diff with the config delta that explains it"
description: "Diff two runs at the metric level and report the hyperparameter, environment-version and reward-spec delta alongside, because a metric difference with no configuration difference beside it is not an explanation."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-07-31T06:38:37.499Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-16T02:15:03.674Z"
assignee: pi-agent
claim_principal: pi-agent
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 360
acceptance_criteria: Reports per-metric differences over the common step range and the full config delta; refuses to compare runs from different environment versions without saying so explicitly
dependencies[1]{id,kind,created_at,author,source_kind,author_source}:
  pm-rl-e20d,parent,"2026-07-31T06:38:37.886Z","harness:claude-code","cli:update:dep",detected
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-16T02:15:03.674Z",pi-agent,"Design decision: comparability refusals are typed and ordered — a run with no recorded environment refuses with run_environment_unrecorded (undecidable), and differing environments refuse with environment_version_mismatch naming both runs and both environment ids. Metric diff is restricted to the intersection of the two runs' measured step spans; zero overlap reports common_step_range null rather than refusing, because an explicitly empty range is honest while only a cross-version diff is misleading. Config delta is computed from each run's recorded body fences (environment snapshot + run configuration), not assumed equal."
body: ""
